    pass-sequence: the workbook builder takes two to six surface columns (a fourth lane for CloudBQ's pass 3)
    
    build_surfaces_xlsx.py refused anything but exactly three surfaces; the Layers and Pipeline steps sheets now carry one column per
    id under `surfaces:` (two to six), the Overview's COUNTIF formulas and --verify locate the Parity column from the header, the
    equality checks keep "first surface vs all the others" keyed by the remaining ids joined ("BC", "BCR", "QW"; "BC" still accepted).
    The three existing specs rebuild to value-identical workbooks (--compare). Reference page updated. Project-agnostic: nothing in the
    script names a repository or a lane. Mirrored in IC-DBT-BQ.
    
